tory\nL45: \nL46: First Known Use\nL47: \nL48: circa 1770, in the meaning defined 【18†above】\nL49: \nL50: Time Traveler\nL51: \nL52: The first known use of civil service was circa 1770\nL53: \nL54: 【19†See more words from the same year】\nL55: \nL56: ## Browse Nearby Words\nL57: \nL58: 【20†civil servant】\nL59: \nL60: civil service\nL61: \nL62: 【21†civil service exam】\nL63: \nL64: 【22†See all Nearby Words】\nL65: ## Cite this Entry\nL66: \nL67: Style\nL68: \nL69: [Select]\nL70: \nL71: “Civil service.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/civil%20service. Accessed 27 Oct. 2026.\nL72: \nL73: 【23†Image†prod.cdn-mw.com】Copy Citation\nL74: \nL75: ## Kids Definition\nL76: \nL77: civil service\nL78: \nL79: noun\nL80: \nL81: : the branch of a government that takes care of the business of running a state but that does not include the lawmaking branch, the military, or the court system\nL82: ## More from Merriam-Webster on civil service\nL83: \nL84: Britannica.com: 【24†Encyclopedia article about civil service†www.britannica.com】\nL85: \nL86: Love words? Need even more definitions?\nL87: \nL88: Subscribe to America's largest dictionary and get thousands more definitions and advanced search—ad free!\nL89: \nL90: Last Updated: 30 Sep 2026 - Updated example sentences\nL91: \nL92: ## More from Merriam-Webster\nL93: \nL94: #### 【3†Word of the Day】\nL95: \nL96: #### 【3†milieu】\nL97: \nL98: 【3†See Definitions and Examples】 »\nL99: ## Popular in Grammar & Usage\nL100: \nL101: 【4†See More】\nL102: \nL103: 【25†Merriam-Webster’s Great Big List of Words You Love to Hate】\nL104: \nL105: 【26†'Can' vs. 'May'】\nL106: \nL107: 【27†'Affect' vs. 'Effect'】\nL108: \nL109: 【28†More Commonly Mispronounced Words】\nL110: \nL111: 【29†'A' or 'an'? What about before 'h'? An Indefinite Article Guide】\nL112: ## Popular in Wordplay\nL113: \nL114: 【8†See More】\nL115: \nL116: 【30†The Longest Long Words List】\nL117: \nL118: 【31†9 Words That Sound Like Insults B